## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
 ASE Technology Holding → Supplies advanced packaging services to AMD → Drives scale and pricing power → Higher margins fund R&D investments → Reinforces ASX’s position as a critical supplier in the AI semiconductor ecosystem.  

**Durability Verdict:** Moderate — ASX benefits from secular AI-driven demand but faces execution risks.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
ASX is fab-lite, relying on foundries for production, which exposes it to capacity constraints and rising costs during upcycles. Its customer concentration in the data center market (via AMD) introduces risk if demand slows.  

**Severity:** **MEDIUM** — Foundry dependency and customer concentration create vulnerability to cyclical downturns.  

